Arbace's variant of hamcrest-core 1.3's sources (org.hamcrest:hamcrest-core:1.3, its sources jar; BSD-3, LICENSE.md
"Hamcrest"): the two calls jdk26u's javac (javac on Arbace, at release 25) rejects for a wildcard's capture, AnyOf's and
AllOf's varargs factories passing Arrays.asList(matchers) to their Iterable overload, given their type argument
explicitly. No behaviour changes. That the JDK's own javac rejects them too is to be confirmed at the oracle tier (the
night slot ghidra-g1b's oracle step). Applied by bin/java-project (program.edn :patches, -p1 over the unpacked sources).

--- a/org/hamcrest/core/AllOf.java
+++ b/org/hamcrest/core/AllOf.java
@@ -57,7 +57,7 @@
      */
     @Factory
     public static <T> Matcher<T> allOf(Matcher<? super T>... matchers) {
-        return allOf(Arrays.asList(matchers));
+        return allOf(Arrays.<Matcher<? super T>>asList(matchers));
     }
 
     /**
--- a/org/hamcrest/core/AnyOf.java
+++ b/org/hamcrest/core/AnyOf.java
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@
      */
     @Factory
     public static <T> AnyOf<T> anyOf(Matcher<? super T>... matchers) {
-        return anyOf(Arrays.asList(matchers));
+        return anyOf(Arrays.<Matcher<? super T>>asList(matchers));
     }
 
